# Trivy policy exceptions — the ONLY sanctioned way past the blocking scans in ci.yml.
# Every entry carries: finding id, one-line justification, owner, and the date added.
# This file is applied ONLY to the blocking gate scans; the SARIF reports uploaded to
# the Security tab stay unfiltered, so ignored findings remain visible there.
#
# ---- Image CVE gate (severity CRITICAL,HIGH, ignore-unfixed) ------------------------
# 2026-07-06: the Spring Boot 3.5.16 bump (PRs #25-#29) cleared the six previously
# waived Spring/Tomcat CRITICALs, so those entries are gone. The rebuilt images carry
# 0 CRITICAL and 0 HIGH in our Java dependencies and OS packages.
#
# The eight HIGHs below all live in the /usr/bin/pebble Go binary shipped inside the
# CURRENT eclipse-temurin:21-jre base image — not in our code or our dependencies.
# pebble is Canonical's service manager, baked into the Ubuntu base layer; we do not
# invoke it and cannot patch it. Every one is a Go standard-library CVE in the
# toolchain pebble was compiled with (go1.26.5), all fixed upstream in Go 1.26.6, so
# the fix has to arrive as a temurin base rebuilt on that toolchain. Owner: devops.
#
# 2026-08-25: upstream rebuilt the whole temurin fleet on 2026-08-21 and pebble moved
# go1.26.3 -> go1.26.5. That retired seven of the eight waivers carried since July,
# which are deleted here rather than left to empty the gate for ids that no longer
# match anything. The same rebuild did NOT reach Go 1.26.6, so seven newly disclosed
# stdlib CVEs took their place. Verified on the image the gate actually scans, built
# from main 905dce6: an unfiltered scan reports exactly the eight ids below.
#
# REMOVAL CONDITION: delete every entry in this block once eclipse-temurin:21-jre
# ships a pebble built with Go 1.26.6 or newer. Check the shipped toolchain with:
#   docker run --rm eclipse-temurin:21-jre \
#     grep -a -o -E 'go1\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+' /usr/bin/pebble
# Ids are listed one by one on purpose — never widen this to a pattern, or the next
# pebble CVE is absorbed silently instead of turning the gate red.
# Watchdog: the weekly scheduled-image-scan workflow runs report-only with NO
# ignorefile, so these findings stay visible there week over week; re-check this
# block on every base-image refresh.
#
# Standing alternative, if upstream keeps lagging (backlog #26): eclipse-temurin
# 21-jre-noble and 21-jre-alpine ship NO pebble binary at all, so moving the five
# Java runtime stages off the default tag would delete this block outright. That is
# a fleet-wide base change needing its own slice and a full rebuild + test pass, not
# a waiver edit.

